      "writtenOn": "2025-05-06T16:57:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like Vulkan itself does not enforce that only one value within `VkDebugUtilsMessageSeverityFlagBitsEXT` is set. At a minimum, we may want to have an `else` that `SkASSERT`s to false if multiple severities are set just to catch the case where this may occur. \n\nhttps://registry.khronos.org/vulkan/specs/latest/man/html/VkDebugUtilsMessageSeverityFlagBitsEXT.html\n\nThough I am in agreement that in this case we should just print out the most severe level. So perhaps return to using `\u0026` as opposed to `\u003d\u003d` for severity values?\n\nDo we want to check for `VK_DEBUG_UTILS_MESSAGE_SEVERITY_VERBOSE_BIT_EXT`?",
      "parentUuid": "2bb527e9_5001f64f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 144,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 151,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "f3e0bd070fe3b521ea387681628a5cbff97974da",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "71211150_15f3f7ee",
        "filename": "tools/gpu/vk/VkTestUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 151,
      "author": {
        "id": 20444
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-06T17:25:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So for severity, it\u0027s ensured by the fact that the parameter is `VkDebugUtilsMessageSeverityFlagBitsEXT` and not `VkDebugUtilsMessageSeverityFlagsEXT`. I know C doesn\u0027t strongly type-check this stuff, but a parameter of `VkDebugUtilsMessageSeverityFlagBitsEXT` is supposed to have only one bit in it.\n\nI went back to `\u0026` just in case anyway. As for VERBOSE, we\u0027ll output `message` (if ever enabled, currently they are not)!",
      "parentUuid": "8aba0a1e_2ea85eb8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 144,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 151,
        "endChar": 5
      },
